        "body": "Serve Robotics is a self-driving delivery company whose website frames its work around the last-mile problem, asking why a 2-pound burrito should move in a 2-ton car. It describes its robot, Serve, as a low-emissions alternative for local delivery, and says it is setting the standard for safety on and beyond the sidewalk, protecting customer data, employees, and the public. The site also describes the company as already a pop culture icon and notes that its robot Saymo appears as John Mulaney's sidekick on the show \"Everybody's Live.\"\n\nThe company is a public company headquartered in San Carlos, California, trading under the ticker SERV, with CIK 0001832483.\n\nIts litigation record lists no cases. Its law exposure listing is concentrated in California, with a count of 281. No products and no MCP servers are tracked for it.",
